.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-MAC 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-mac
.Nd perform Message Authentication Code operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl mac
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl cipher ]
.Oo
.Fl digest ]
.Oo
.Fl macopt ]
.Oo
.Fl in
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl out
.Em filename ]
.Oo
.Fl binary ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Em mac_name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The message authentication code functions output the MAC of a supplied
input file.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print a usage message.
.It Sy -in Em filename
Input filename to calculate a MAC for, or standard input by default.
Standard input is used if the filename is '-'. Files and standard input
are expected to be in binary format.
.It Sy -out Em filename
Filename to output to, or standard output by default.
.It Sy -binary
Output the MAC in binary form.
Uses hexadecimal text format if not specified.
.It Sy -cipher Em name
Used by CMAC and GMAC to specify the cipher algorithm.
For CMAC it should be a CBC mode cipher e.g.
AES-128-CBC. For GMAC it should be a GCM mode cipher e.g.
AES-128-GCM.
.It Sy -digest Em name
Used by HMAC as an alphanumeric string (use if the key contains
printable characters only).
The string length must conform to any restrictions of the MAC algorithm.
To see the list of supported digests, use
.Qo Li openssl list -digest-commands Qc .
.It Sy -macopt Em nm Ns : Ns Em v
Passes options to the MAC algorithm.
A comprehensive list of controls can be found in the EVP_MAC
implementation documentation.
Common parameter names used by
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3
are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy key: Ns Em string
Specifies the MAC key as an alphanumeric string (use if the key contains
printable characters only).
The string length must conform to any restrictions of the MAC algorithm.
A key must be specified for every MAC algorithm.
.It Sy hexkey: Ns Em string
Specifies the MAC key in hexadecimal form (two hex digits per byte).
The key length must conform to any restrictions of the MAC algorithm.
A key must be specified for every MAC algorithm.
.It Sy iv: Ns Em string
Used by GMAC to specify an IV as an alphanumeric string (use if the IV
contains printable characters only).
.It Sy hexiv: Ns Em string
Used by GMAC to specify an IV in hexadecimal form (two hex digits per
byte).
.It Sy size: Ns Em int
Used by KMAC128 or KMAC256 to specify an output length.
The default sizes are 32 or 64 bytes respectively.
.It Sy custom: Ns Em string
Used by KMAC128 or KMAC256 to specify a customization string.
The default is the empty string "".
.It Sy digest: Ns Em string
This option is identical to the
.Sy -digest
option.
.It Sy cipher: Ns Em string
This option is identical to the
.Sy -cipher
option.
.El
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.It Em mac_name
Specifies the name of a supported MAC algorithm which will be used.
To see the list of supported MAC's use the command
.Qo Li openssl list -mac-algorithms Qc .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
To create a hex-encoded HMAC-SHA1 MAC of a file and write to stdout:
.Bd -literal
 openssl mac -digest SHA1 \e
         -macopt hexkey:000102030405060708090A0B0C0D0E0F10111213 \e
         -in msg.bin HMAC
.Ed
.Pp
To create a SipHash MAC from a file with a binary file output:
.Bd -literal
 openssl mac -macopt hexkey:000102030405060708090A0B0C0D0E0F \e
         -in msg.bin -out out.bin -binary SipHash
.Ed
.Pp
To create a hex-encoded CMAC-AES-128-CBC MAC from a file:
.Bd -literal
 openssl mac -cipher AES-128-CBC \e
         -macopt hexkey:77A77FAF290C1FA30C683DF16BA7A77B \e
         -in msg.bin CMAC
.Ed
.Pp
To create a hex-encoded KMAC128 MAC from a file with a Customisation
String 'Tag' and output length of 16:
.Bd -literal
 openssl mac -macopt custom:Tag -macopt hexkey:40414243444546 \e
         -macopt size:16 -in msg.bin KMAC128
.Ed
.Pp
To create a hex-encoded GMAC-AES-128-GCM with a IV from a file:
.Bd -literal
 openssl mac -cipher AES-128-GCM -macopt hexiv:E0E00F19FED7BA0136A797F3 \e
         -macopt hexkey:77A77FAF290C1FA30C683DF16BA7A77B -in msg.bin GMAC
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
The MAC mechanisms that are available will depend on the options used
when building OpenSSL. Use
.Qo Li openssl list -mac-algorithms Qc
to list them.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC-CMAC 7 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC-GMAC 7 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC-HMAC 7 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC-KMAC 7 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC-Siphash 7 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC-Poly1305 7
